depgraph: one-node shortcut in find_smallest_cycle

Sub-series: B (cycle search and frontier) - patch 3 of 6; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs none: it also applies to 3.0.83 by itself.

A candidate with no child at the current level is its own closure, and
no closure is smaller than one node, so the search can stop there.
Alone on 3.0.83: start 119.6 -> 110.0; no effect on short merge lists.
Read, not tested: nodes with a self-edge never become candidates.
Applies to upstream head unchanged.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
